  "term": "cirrhosis",
  "definition": "Cirrhosis is a disorder in which normal liver tissue is replaced by scar-like fibrous tissue and regenerative nodules. It is commonly linked to alcohol use and hepatitis B or C, and it can lead to fluid buildup in the abdomen, enlarged veins in the esophagus, bleeding, and problems with brain function caused by liver disease.",
